design:
Semantic-system design/evaluation only. Test the compositional reconstruction hypothesis before proposing storage:

- generic Eshyra DM charter;
- optional bounded campaign/table-specific DM charter;
- authoritative campaign/module/rules/state and campaign rulings;
- bounded generated campaign/character memory;
- optional latest bounded outgoing handoff;
- fresh provider-neutral model invocation occupying the persistent institutional DM role.

Use a four-arm ablation: A current baseline; B baseline + standing campaign/table charter; C baseline + outgoing handoff; D baseline + both. Define independent, falsifiable measures for behavioral/table continuity, narrative salience, non-restatement, authority compliance, stale-evidence handling, context cost, and provider/model-change robustness. Include normal close/resume and hard fresh-context cases. Reuse existing context, evaluation, trace, and audit seams where practical; ADR 0017 section 8 forbids a parallel proof system with no distinct failure class.

A seat is a conceptual composition unless evidence demonstrates a concrete producer/consumer/lifecycle that cannot be represented by existing or narrowly extended prompt, preference, memory, and provenance primitives. The investigation may conclude that campaign-specific style continuity has product value; it may not turn style, preference, or handoff intent into canon or rules authority. Evaluate the auditor independently and preserve its constrained mechanics/state jurisdiction.
